  "question": {
    "text": "A lens forms a real image of an object at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. It is observed that on placing another identical lens in contact with it, the image gets shifted by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> towards the combination. The power of the lens is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#xA0;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2.5</mn><mi>&#xA0;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>&#xA0;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#xA0;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
